 2. 🏒 Ovi&#x27;s last dance 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Alexander Ovechkin ahead of an April 2025 game against the Carolina Hurricanes. Photo: Patrick Smith/Getty Images Alexander Ovechkin, the "Great 8," is calling it a career after this season, Axios D.C.'s Mark Selig reports. 

 🥅 The NHL's all-time leading goal-scorer has been the face of hockey's Washington Capitals for more than two decades, transforming them into one of D.C.'s most consistently relevant pro teams.

 He delivered the Caps' first Stanley Cup in 2018, rewrote the NHL record book and became one of the most recognizable athletes in Washington sports history. Ovechkin told teammates today: "This is going to be my last year."

 "It's hard, but let's enjoy it and let's do some special things this year." 🇷🇺 Between the lines: Ovechkin's announcement comes amid controversy over his outspoken support for Russian President Vladimir Putin.

