 3. ⚡️ Catch me up 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Lab workers at the Russia-based Irkutsk Anti-Plague Research Institute of Siberia and the Far East. Photo: AP 🦠 Russian authorities quarantined a hospital and are monitoring contacts of a Siberian plague research institute employee who contracted pneumonia from an "unknown" cause. Local state TV said the woman died last week. What to know . 🧠 The Nobel Prize in medicine was awarded to three scientists whose work led to a tool that uses light to help unravel how the brain works. Two are German and one, Dr. Karl Deisseroth , 54, is a Stanford professor. Read the announcement . ✈️ The White House is barring Politico from boarding Air Force One today, CNN reports — the latest in an ongoing battle between the press and the Trump administration. Go deeper . 🗳️ House Majority Whip Tom Emmer (R-Minn.) is scaling back expectations and zeroing in on a narrowed battlefield as Republicans' prospects of keeping their majority look increasingly bleak. More from Axios' Kate Santaliz . 🏛️ Dennis Hastert — the longest-serving Republican speaker of the House, who later admitted to sexually abusing teenage wrestlers and was imprisoned on charges tied to hush-money payments — died Saturday at 84 at his home in Plano, Ill., under hospice care. N.Y. Times obit . 
 
